================================================================================
## Address review on Graph Chat max_tokens (PR follow-ups)
================================================================================

Context: Review on the Graph Chat `max_tokens` PR. The branch was rebased onto
`0.9.3` (0.9.2 was merged and archived), so the changelog moved to
`changelogs/v0.9.3/`. The engine default and the `Settings` default could drift
apart; the env var sat in the analytics test map and docs table; the setting had
no bounds although Foundation Model endpoints cap output at ~8192 tokens.

Changes:

1. src/shared/config/constants.py
   New `DTWIN_CHAT_MAX_TOKENS = 8192`, the single source of truth for the default and ceiling.
2. src/shared/config/settings.py
   `dtwin_chat_max_tokens` defaults to the constant and is bounded `ge=1, le=8192`.
3. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py
   `DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS` now derives from the shared constant.
4. app.yaml.template
   Comment states the default is also the maximum.
5. docs/getting-started.md
   Move the env var into a new "Graph Chat (Digital Twin Assistant)" subsection; document bounds.
6. tests/units/settings/test_app_yaml_template.py
   Split `DTWIN_CHAT_VARS` / `TestDtwinChatDefaultsMatchSettings` out of the analytics map; reject out-of-bounds values.
7. tests/units/agents/test_agent_dtwin_chat_engine.py
   Assert engine and `Settings` defaults match; override test uses 4096 (within the ceiling).
8. changelogs/v0.9.3/diegoantonelli_2026-11-06.log
   Moved from `changelogs/v0.9.1/` to match the target release.

